   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** makes a picture from text with LongCat-Image (6B, Apache-2.0), good at readable text. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Prompt**: describe the picture. Text that must appear goes in \"quotes\".\n   - **Negative prompt**: things to avoid. It is the template's list without `text` and `logo`, which work against signs.\n   - **Picture shape**: aspect ratio and megapixels. 3:2 at 1 megapixel gives 1248x832.\n   - **Steps** (20): the template value, 46 to 48 s here. The authors use 50 (110 s); 30 took 67 to 69 s. All three gave a similar picture.\n   - **CFG** (4): the template's and the authors' value.\n   - **Seed**: fixed at 25112026. Type a new number for another picture; Run with nothing changed does nothing.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note.\n3. **Prompt + size**: nothing to change.\n4. **Sampling**: euler / simple with CFG norm 1. Nothing to change.\n5. **Save**: press **Run**. The picture is saved to `output/LongCat/`.\n\n**What to expect:** a 1248x832 picture in 46 to 48 s on the test card (20 steps).\nThe sign was spelled right on 5 of 6 seeds at 20 steps (seed 777 wrote LONIGCAT); small background signs are often nonsense. Wrong spelling: try another seed.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, 64 GB RAM, ComfyUI 0.45.3. Not verified on a 12 GB card.\n"
   ]
  },
